WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.330
This story is one of those stories where you
really have to look at the details to know

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.240
what what is the story?

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.340
Is this a big story or not?

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:13.980
The the story is that Democratic vice presidential
nominee Kamala Harris has now confirmed that

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:21.050
if she and Joe Biden are elected, that they
would decriminalize the use of marijuana at

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:22.260
the federal level.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.610
Now, everybody went crazy for different reasons.

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:30.610
Kamala Harris outlined at an event through
Facebook Live with ABC.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.300
The broad strokes of the proposal.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:39.250
And it includes, among other things, which
I will get to full federal decriminalization

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.730
of the use of marijuana.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:46.480
You had some people on the right who are just
furious, who say decriminalizing marijuana

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.260
use is the first step to anarchy.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.190
It's the first step to rampant out of control,
addiction and chaos everywhere.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.690
Biden must be stopped.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:58.350
And then you have people on the left who are
saying, this is so lame.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.900
This is so centrist.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.899
Decriminalize use.

00:01:01.899 --> 00:01:03.770
We must legalize use.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:07.160
We must decriminalize small scale dealing
of marijuana.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.240
This is way too right wing for me.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.070
So what's the truth?

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:16.780
The truth is one that most people don't want
to accept, which is progress typically comes

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:17.780
in steps.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:23.680
I believe we need full legalization of use,
regulate it, tax it.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.700
Selling it on the street becomes sort of like
selling illegal cigarets and you deal with

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:33.180
it like a health issue instead of a criminal
issue when you have substance abuse issues.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:39.580
Without question, though, a federal decriminalization
would be a big deal, but it would just be

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:43.119
one step with another four years of Trump.

00:01:43.119 --> 00:01:45.040
We get nothing.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.040
We just get nothing.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.479
Simply nothing, period.

00:01:47.479 --> 00:01:53.439
Now, there are also people mad that a flip
flopped Comilla used to be against legalization

00:01:53.439 --> 00:01:56.640
and decriminalization 10 years ago.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.590
Well, she's changed her view and we should
applaud that.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:04.610
In other words, there are lots of elected
officials who eventually came around to better

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:08.019
positions and they shouldn't be shamed for
that.

00:02:08.019 --> 00:02:12.889
Some, what some people call flip flopping
sometimes is flip flopping merely for for

00:02:12.889 --> 00:02:14.989
sort of political posturing purposes.

00:02:14.989 --> 00:02:19.310
But sometimes you evolve because you actually
get more information or you mature.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:21.999
You come around to the right point of view.

00:02:21.999 --> 00:02:28.409
So when 2019, she sponsored legislation which
would federally d schedule cannabis, that

00:02:28.409 --> 00:02:31.230
would would be a great thing to do.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.700
And overall, we should be glad that she changed
her mind.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.280
Now, let's be real.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.870
There is a major gap between decriminalization
and legalization.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:47.329
If you legalize cannabis, you can regulate
it similar to alcohol and tobacco.

00:02:47.329 --> 00:02:55.139
You can tax it to decriminalize cannabis merely
removes criminal sanctions when you offend

00:02:55.139 --> 00:02:57.180
or break the law.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.439
Cannabis could remain illegal.

00:02:59.439 --> 00:03:05.499
Possession above a certain amount could result
in civil fines or drug education or treatment

00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:07.499
instead of criminal prosecution.

00:03:07.499 --> 00:03:09.269
So it is not a panacea.

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:13.019
It is not the end point, but it is a step
forward.

00:03:13.019 --> 00:03:19.879
Joe Biden, by the way, wouldn't just federally,
federally decriminalize, but according to

00:03:19.879 --> 00:03:26.459
his Web site, would are also expunge prior
cannabis use convictions.

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:27.629
That's a good thing.

00:03:27.629 --> 00:03:30.029
That gets a bunch of people cleared.

00:03:30.029 --> 00:03:35.809
It's certainly not going to impact low level
dealers who are sitting in prison.

00:03:35.809 --> 00:03:38.249
And we need to deal with that.

00:03:38.249 --> 00:03:39.249
But it is a step forward.

00:03:39.249 --> 00:03:45.280
Joe Biden also supports the legalization of
medical cannabis at the federal level, but

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:51.849
again, would leave decisions about adult recreational
use up to the states.

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:57.529
So, listen, this is one of those times where
we just have to be very real and pragmatic.

00:03:57.529 --> 00:04:03.590
If Biden gets to do what is on his platform,
it would be the most progressive federal cannabis

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:06.650
policy in the history of a sitting president,
period.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:08.669
I get that we want to do more.

00:04:08.669 --> 00:04:12.599
I get that many of us feel that it's 20/20
and this is not enough.

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:17.170
And we need to be catching up to other countries
that have dealt with this in in more progressive

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:18.680
ways already.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:24.800
But if Biden gets in and he does this stuff,
the U.S. would be as progressive at as it

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:30.540
has ever been when it comes to the regulation
of cannabis.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:36.900
If they do this, it will lead to more legalization
in more states for sure.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:44.760
There will be states who, if they see, decriminalized
federally expunging convictions, so on and

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.760
so forth.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:52.020
There will be states that maybe right now
are 53 to 47 against legalization that will

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.490
say look at look what's happening federally.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:55.490
Let's do it.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:59.760
You know, other states have done it, Massachusetts
did it, Colorado, etc., this will be a major

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:00.770
step forward.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:03.700
And of course, we want more, but let's not
miss the forest for the trees.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.490
And much like with health care, is Biden's
idea perfect?

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:07.950
Of course not.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:12.900
Does Biden's platform on health care fix all
of the problems we've identified?

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:14.410
Not even close.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:19.530
But if Trump got his way, 30 million people
would lose coverage.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.100
OK, let's not miss the forest for the trees.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:25.970
We're going to have more on this on our Instagram
account.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.830
Follow us there at David Pakman show.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:35.060
Follow me on Instagram at David Pakman for
pictures from my vacation, which I will talk

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:35.450
about on today's bonus show,

